  "modified": "2026-10-06T15:17:05Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-5870: prevent integer overflow in the pixel offset calculations of\n  SkReadPixelsRec/SkWritePixelsRec by routing them through SkSafeMath\n- CVE-2026-7920: stop getRPProgram() mutating the shared SkSL program, which\n  raced with the Ganesh backend reading it and freed IR nodes under it\n- CVE-2026-7923: fix the discard_stack guard in the SkSL raster pipeline\n  builder so it no longer removes more stack entries than the op pushed\n- CVE-2026-10009: bound the number of partial contours in SkPathWriter::assemble\n  so the folded-triangle entry count can no longer overflow\n- CVE-2026-11663: replace the single shared glyph-run builder on SkCanvas with\n  a stack of builders, drop drawable serialization from SkCustomTypeface and\n  restrict the tags deserialized from SkPictures\n- All five are backports into the vendored Skia only; no public API or ABI of\n  the package is touched.",
